6. Cookie consent and Google Analytics

Implement a genuine consent-management experience appropriate to the actual technologies and applicable legal requirements.

Requirements

- Present a clear, accessible cookie-consent interface.
- Offer equivalent, easy-to-understand choices for accepting and rejecting non-essential technologies where required.
- Provide a settings interface for granular choices by category where appropriate.
- Provide a persistent way to reopen preferences.
- Explain categories in plain language.
- Store the consent decision and relevant policy/version information.
- Avoid requesting consent repeatedly when a valid choice remains applicable.
- Allow users to withdraw or change consent.
- Do not use deceptive design, preselected optional categories, or forced acceptance.
- Ensure keyboard accessibility, screen-reader labels, mobile responsiveness, and light/dark theme compatibility.
- Avoid unnecessarily blocking essential website functionality.

Google Analytics 4

Inspect the existing Google Analytics integration before modifying it.

- Preserve the existing verified GA4 measurement ID and its configuration source.
- Never replace a real identifier with an invented example.
