- Ensure the default consent state is applied before analytics tags or related tracking requests execute.
- Ensure that a rejection or withdrawal actually changes subsequent tracking behavior.
- Verify the behavior of Google tags, cookies, and network requests in the browser.
- Do not claim that rejecting consent stops all tracking unless that has been verified.
- Avoid duplicate Google Analytics initialization and duplicate page-view events.
- Preserve existing production analytics data and avoid sending real test-customer data.

If an integration cannot be configured safely without owner authorization or a verified account setting, document the required action rather than guessing.

